        "comments": "The assembly keSacKowa6.1 is based on 35x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Wellcome Sanger Institute Tree of Life Programme (https://www.sanger.ac.uk/programme/tree-of-life/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS, homology based scaffolding to the primary assembly using RagTag. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi and OATK. Finally, the primary assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. This alternate haplotype assembly combines the haplotigs separated by the assembler with haplotigs separated from the primary assembly during curation. A large number of centromeric repeats is in the unlocalised sequences. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 5 (9.3 Mbp - 10.5 Mbp), chromosome 12 (6.0 Mbp - 6.9 Mbp) are unknown.",
